<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεύω</span></b> , = sq. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> intr., <i>turn</i> or <i>go about,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ἄστυ π.</span>
			<i>go about</i> the city, i.e. live therein, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.223
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ πολεύων,</span> in Astrol.,
				<i>the planet presiding over a day,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Serapio
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				1.99
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Leid.W.</u>
				5.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Al.
				<u>I.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψῃ τοὺς πολεύοντας ἀναβαίνοντας εἰς
					οὐρανὸν θεούς, ἄλλους δὲ καταβαίνοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMag.Par.</u>
					1.545
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Myst.</u>
				3.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>turn up</i> the soil with the plough, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶν . . ἱππείῳ γένει π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					341
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).—Poet. and late Prose.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
